    <region left="20" top="2952" width="1560" height="27" color="#0f2a44" fontSize="12" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-size: 12px;">L6  the TI app note idiom      one index, augment(), eval()</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="2987" width="1560" height="51" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">SMPS_Input_Filter_Design_TI_APP_Note.sm fills COLUMN VECTORS with a single index - el(f, j), not el(f, j, 1) - and then glues them with eval(augment(vectorize(x), vectorize(y))). Three differences from L1 at once, but every one of them is taken from a sheet</p>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">that renders here. It also proves eval, augment and vectorize exist, which this project had assumed they did not.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="3046" width="470" height="25" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- fill two column vectors:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="3046" width="760" height="200" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math>
      <input>
        <e type="operand">k.6</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operand">N.2</e>
        <e type="function" args="2">range</e>
        <e type="operand">X.6</e>
        <e type="operand">k.6</e>
        <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
        <e type="operand">0.55</e>
        <e type="operand">k.6</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
        <e type="bracket">(</e>
        <e type="operand">1.65</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operand">N.2</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">+</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        <e type="operand">Y.6</e>
        <e type="operand">k.6</e>
        <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operand">λ</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">+</e>
        <e type="operand">λ</e>
        <e type="operand">X.6</e>
        <e type="operand">k.6</e>
        <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
        <e type="operand">2</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">^</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
        <e type="bracket">(</e>
        <e type="operand">2</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">^</e>
        <e type="operand">Q.c</e>
        <e type="operand">2</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">^</e>
        <e type="operand">X.6</e>
        <e type="operand">k.6</e>
        <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operand">X.6</e>
        <e type="operand">k.6</e>
        <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
        <e type="bracket">(</e>
        <e type="operand">2</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">^</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">+</e>
        <e type="function" args="1">sqrt</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        <e type="operand">2</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="function" args="4">line</e>
        <e type="function" args="3">for</e>
      </input>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="3254" width="470" height="25" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- Y.6 last point, gain must be 0.5096:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="510" top="3254" width="1080" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="8" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="4">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">r.6b</e>
        <e type="operand">Y.6</e>
        <e type="operand">N.2</e>
        <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">0.5096</e>
        </result>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="3291" width="470" height="25" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- glue them the way the TI sheet does:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="3316" width="760" height="64" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="4" exponentialThreshold="5">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">P.6</e>
        <e type="operand">X.6</e>
        <e type="function" args="1">vectorize</e>
        <e type="operand">Y.6</e>
        <e type="function" args="1">vectorize</e>
        <e type="function" args="2">augment</e>
        <e type="function" args="1">eval</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="3388" width="520" height="260" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <plot grid="true" axes="true" type="2d" render="lines" scale_x="0.013461538" scale_y="0.030769231" scale_z="1" rotate_x="0" rotate_y="0" rotate_z="0" transpose_x="-409" transpose_y="-130" transpose_z="0">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">P.6</e>
      </input>
    </plot>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="3696" width="1560" height="27" color="#0f2a44" fontSize="12" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-size: 12px;">L7  no matrix at all      plot a FUNCTION of the plot variable</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="3731" width="1560" height="51" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">Project Admittance Copy.sm puts S1(x) and S2(x) straight into a plot. For a closed-form gain curve that is the obvious thing to do - no loop, no matrix, nothing to fill - and it was never tried here. If this rung draws and the others do not, the whole</p>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">matrix approach can be dropped.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="3790" width="470" height="25" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 10px;">- define the gain as a function of x:</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="3815" width="760" height="64" isBreakable="false">
    <math decimalPlaces="4" exponentialThreshold="5">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">x</e>
        <e type="function" args="1">M.f</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operand">λ</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">+</e>
        <e type="operand">λ</e>
        <e type="operand">x</e>
        <e type="operand">2</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">^</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
        <e type="bracket">(</e>
        <e type="operand">2</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">^</e>
        <e type="operand">Q.c</e>
        <e type="operand">2</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">^</e>
        <e type="operand">x</e>
        <e type="operand">1</e>
        <e type="operand">x</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
        <e type="bracket">(</e>
        <e type="operand">2</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">^</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">+</e>
        <e type="function" args="1">sqrt</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
        <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
      </input>
    </math>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="3887" width="1560" height="23" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">- M.f(1) must be 1.0000 whatever Q, and M.f(2.20) must be 0.5096.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="3918" width="520" height="260" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <plot grid="true" axes="true" type="2d" render="lines" scale_x="0.013461538" scale_y="0.030769231" scale_z="1" rotate_x="0" rotate_y="0" rotate_z="0" transpose_x="-409" transpose_y="-130" transpose_z="0">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">x</e>
        <e type="function" args="1">M.f</e>
      </input>
    </plot>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="4226" width="1560" height="27" color="#0f2a44" fontSize="12" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; font-size: 12px;">L5  the same T.1 at four grid divisions      only one window can be right</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="4261" width="1560" height="23" color="#444444" fontSize="9" isBreakable="false">
    <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
      <content>
        <p style="font-weight: normal; font-style: normal; font-size: 9px;">If L1 printed its numbers but drew nothing, the matrix is fine and the window is not. These four ask for the identical window and differ only in the pixels per grid division: 20, 8, 4, 2 - left to right, top row then bottom.</p>
      </content>
    </text>
    </region>
    <region left="20" top="4292" width="520" height="260" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <plot grid="true" axes="true" type="2d" render="lines" scale_x="0.067307692" scale_y="0.153846154" scale_z="1" rotate_x="0" rotate_y="0" rotate_z="0" transpose_x="-409" transpose_y="-130" transpose_z="0">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">T.1</e>
      </input>
    </plot>
    </region>
    <region left="580" top="4292" width="520" height="260" color="#000000" fontSize="10" isBreakable="false">
    <plot grid="true" axes="true" type="2d" render="lines" scale_x="0.026923077" scale_y="0.061538462" scale_z="1" rotate_x="0" rotate_y="0" rotate_z="0" transpose_x="-409" transpose_y="-130" transpose_z="0">
      <input>
        <e type="operand">T.1</e>
      </input>
    </plot>
